# AI Agent Development Brief: Template-to-Flyer Generator App

## 1. Product vision

Create an app that allows a user to quickly build rough visual templates for flyers, adverts, inventory boards, catalogs, menus, event posters, service listings, comparison charts, and social posts.

The app should not try to be Photoshop, Canva, or Illustrator. Its purpose is to make it very fast to organize content, produce a clean rough layout, and then pass that layout to an AI image generator with detailed prompt instructions to create a polished professional visual design.

The attached handgun inventory board is the reference workflow:

1. User enters structured item data.
2. App organizes items into sections and cards.
3. App generates a rough layout that is accurate and readable.
4. User exports the rough layout plus prompt instructions.
5. AI image generator produces a polished visual version.
6. App optionally re-applies exact text/images/prices/contact info on top of the polished design to avoid hallucinated or corrupted details.

The app should support many layouts depending on the number of items, item priority, categories, available images, desired output size, and whether the user wants a dense inventory board, a premium hero flyer, a social ad, or a simple menu/listing.

---

# 2. Core product principle

The app should separate **content truth** from **visual styling**.

## Content truth

This includes:

* Item names
* Prices
* Sale prices
* Categories
* Descriptions
* Badges
* Legal disclaimers
* Phone numbers
* URLs
* Email addresses
* Dates
* Product specs
* QR codes
* Logos
* Contact blocks

These should be generated and rendered deterministically by the app.

## Visual styling

This includes:

* Background texture
* Borders
* Shadows
* Lighting
* Typography style direction
* Decorative framing
* Color palette
* Mood
* Depth
* Premium polish
* Brand atmosphere
* Poster aesthetics

These can be handled by the AI image generator.

## Important design rule

Do **not** rely on the AI image generator to preserve exact text, prices, phone numbers, disclaimers, or URLs. The app should support an “AI polish + exact overlay” workflow where the generated image is used as the styled background/design layer, then the app re-renders exact content on top.

---

# 3. Target users

Primary user:

* Small business owner, club admin, marketer, reseller, event organizer, or operator who needs to create visually appealing flyers quickly.
* User may not be a professional designer.
* User may have many items and photos.
* User needs speed, organization, and repeatable layouts.

Secondary user:

* Technical power user who wants structured data import/export, reusable templates, JSON layout definitions, and AI prompt control.

