## Step 3: Organize content

The app should provide a table/grid interface for managing content.

User can:

* Create sections
* Drag items between sections
* Reorder items
* Mark items as hero, featured, normal, compact, hidden, or footer-only
* Set card size preference
* Set badge text
* Set sale price
* Add notes
* Crop item images
* Choose image fit mode: contain, cover, crop, transparent background, full bleed
* Validate missing fields

The app should make content organization easier than a generic design tool.

---

## Step 4: Choose or generate a rough layout

The user selects a layout family or asks the app to auto-pick.

The app should generate a rough layout using deterministic layout rules, not random image generation.

The rough layout should be clean enough that an AI image generator can understand the structure.

The rough layout should include:

* Header
* Brand area
* Main title
* Subtitle
* Section headers
* Item cards
* Images
* Prices
* Badges
* Footer/contact block
* Legal/disclaimer text
* Safe margins
* Optional QR code block
* Optional sponsor/logo strip

---

## Step 5: Edit the rough layout

Editor should allow:

* Dragging sections
* Dragging cards
* Resizing cards
* Switching a section from 2-column to 3-column
* Promoting an item to hero
* Collapsing a description
* Adjusting density
* Adjusting image/text split
* Changing title/footer size
* Applying brand colors
* Locking critical elements
* Duplicating a layout variant
* Comparing variants side-by-side

The editor should avoid complex freeform design at first. It should be structured, constrained, and fast.

---

## Step 6: Export AI handoff package

The app should export:

1. Rough layout image, PNG
2. Transparent text/content overlay, PNG or SVG
3. Exact content JSON
4. Layout JSON
5. Brand/style JSON
6. Prompt file, Markdown or TXT
7. Optional negative prompt
8. Optional “AI-safe background only” version with text removed
9. Optional PDF proof
10. Optional final composited export

This package should be easy to pass into ChatGPT image generation, Midjourney, Firefly, Ideogram, DALL-E-style tools, or future image APIs.

---

## Step 7: AI polish workflow

Recommended workflow:

1. Export rough layout with exact visual structure.
2. Send rough layout to image generator with prompt instructions.
3. Ask the generator to improve the professional visual design while preserving composition.
4. Generate polished version.
5. Import polished version back into the app.
6. Use the app to overlay exact text, prices, images, QR codes, and disclaimers.
7. Export final PNG/PDF.

This avoids the common problem where the AI-generated image looks great but corrupts product names, prices, or contact details.

