# 7. Adaptive layout behavior

The layout engine should choose layouts based on content count and importance.

Example rules:

| Number of items | Recommended layout                            |
| --------------: | --------------------------------------------- |
|               1 | Premium single-item hero                      |
|               2 | Split feature layout                          |
|               3 | Three-card feature row                        |
|             4-6 | Hero + grid or compact catalog                |
|            7-12 | Sectioned grid                                |
|           13-24 | Dense inventory board                         |
|             25+ | Multi-page catalog or compressed table layout |

The engine should also consider:

* Number of sections
* Longest item name
* Image availability
* Price visibility
* Required footer size
* Legal copy length
* Canvas aspect ratio
* Item priority
* Whether a hero item exists
* Whether any section must stay together

---

# 8. Layout engine requirements

The layout engine should be deterministic and inspectable.

It should accept structured content and return a layout tree with exact positions.

Input:

* Canvas dimensions
* Safe margins
* Brand settings
* Sections
* Items
* Images
* Density setting
* Layout family
* Required footer/header blocks

Output:

* Positioned elements
* Bounding boxes
* Font sizes
* Image crop boxes
* Overflow warnings
* Suggested alternatives
* Export-ready layout JSON

The layout engine should support:

* Grid calculation
* Section packing
* Hero card allocation
* Auto font sizing
* Text truncation rules
* Price alignment
* Image aspect-ratio handling
* Gutters and safe margins
* Minimum readable text size
* Collision detection
* Overflow detection
* Layout scoring

---

## Layout scoring

Each generated layout variant should receive a score.

Possible scoring criteria:

| Criterion                   | Purpose                     |
| --------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| No text overflow            | Prevent broken exports      |
| Minimum font size respected | Keep flyer readable         |
| Balanced whitespace         | Avoid lopsided layouts      |
| Section integrity           | Keep grouped items together |
| Image visibility            | Avoid tiny product images   |
| Price visibility            | Keep price easy to find     |
| Hero priority respected     | Feature important items     |
| Footer/legal retained       | Avoid compliance errors     |
| Prompt clarity              | Make AI handoff easier      |

The app should generate several variants and let the user choose.

