# 16. AI handoff strategy

The app should support three AI handoff modes.

## Mode A: Full visual reference

Use when user wants the AI image generator to polish the whole design.

Input to generator:

* Rough template image
* Detailed visual prompt
* Style references
* Exact content warning

Risk:

* Text may get corrupted.

Best for:

* Concepting
* Quick ads where exact text is not critical
* Layout exploration

---

## Mode B: Background/style-only generation

Recommended default.

The app exports a version of the layout with text removed or reduced to placeholder blocks. The AI generator improves:

* Background
* Borders
* Frames
* Lighting
* Texture
* Decorations
* Overall polish

Then the app overlays the exact text, prices, logos, QR codes, and product photos.

Best for:

* Professional flyers
* Product inventory boards
* Legal/commercial material
* Anything with exact prices/contact info

---

## Mode C: Design concept generation only

The app asks the AI generator for style concepts, then the app recreates the final deterministically.

Best for:

* Brand exploration
* Template creation
* Building reusable styles

---

# 17. Prompt generation requirements

The app should generate a prompt that includes:

* Project type
* Audience
* Brand style
* Canvas format
* Layout preservation instructions
* Section structure
* Visual polish instructions
* Typography direction
* Color palette
* What to change
* What not to change
* Exact text handling rules
* Output quality expectations
* Negative prompt

---

## Example generated AI prompt

```text
Create a polished professional flyer based on the attached rough layout.

Purpose:
A dark tactical-style inventory board with product cards grouped into sections. The layout should remain clearly organized and readable.

Canvas:
Vertical poster format. Preserve the same general composition, section order, item grouping, and footer placement.

Visual direction:
Premium tactical retail board, dark matte background, subtle industrial texture, high contrast, orange accent lines, clean card borders, professional lighting, polished sports/gear catalog aesthetic. Make the design feel finished and commercially usable, similar to a premium retail inventory advertisement.

Layout instructions:
- Keep the large headline area at the top.
- Keep section dividers between groups.
- Keep item cards in a structured grid.
- Keep the premium/used hero item larger near the bottom.
- Keep the footer/contact area at the bottom.
- Preserve spacing hierarchy and readability.
- Improve borders, shadows, background texture, section labels, and overall visual polish.

Critical content instructions:
- Do not invent new products.
- Do not change the number of item cards.
- Do not move products into different sections.
- Do not alter product prices.
- Do not alter phone numbers, emails, website URLs, or legal copy.
- If exact text cannot be preserved, leave text areas clean enough for a deterministic overlay.

Preferred result:
A polished, high-resolution, professional retail flyer/ad design with the same structure as the rough layout, suitable for final text overlay and export.
```

---

## Example negative prompt

```text
Do not create random extra products. Do not add fake logos. Do not distort the layout. Do not create unreadable text. Do not invent contact information. Do not change prices. Do not add cluttered backgrounds. Do not turn product photos into illustrations unless specifically requested. Do not remove footer/legal space.
```

