# 34. Risks and trade-offs

| Risk                                   | Mitigation                                                     |
| -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| AI generator corrupts text             | Use background/style-only generation and exact overlay         |
| Layout engine becomes too complex      | Start with deterministic layout families and simple heuristics |
| User wants too many items on one page  | Warn, reduce density, or suggest multi-page output             |
| Product images have inconsistent sizes | Add crop/focal-point tools and image fit modes                 |
| Templates become hard to maintain      | Use JSON schema and reusable layout primitives                 |
| App becomes a weak Canva clone         | Keep focus on structured content-to-layout workflow            |
| Professional polish varies by AI model | Store reusable prompt presets and style references             |
| Legal/compliance copy omitted          | Treat disclaimers as locked required elements                  |
| Print exports look blurry              | Enforce DPI, image resolution checks, and PDF/SVG output       |

